{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Epic 06: Derivation Recovery and Observability — Test Plan\n     2\t\n     3\t**Companion to:** `tech-design.md` · **Epic:** `epic.md`\n     4\t**Counts:** 39 ACs / 59 TCs across 6 flows, mapped to test files below.\n     5\t\n     6\t## Testing Architecture\n     7\t\n     8\t- **Real storage.** Every test uses a real temp SQLite thread DB (the persistence/atomicity/idempotency contracts are the point — never mock the store).\n     9\t- **One mock boundary.** `DerivationProvider`, via the existing `createDeterministicProvider()` for happy paths and two new doubles for failure paths:\n    10\t  - `failingProvider(opts)` — returns `{ ok:false, retryable }` for a named op, to drive retryable and terminal-failure paths.\n    11\t  - `probingProvider(fn)` — while its call is pending, runs `fn` which attempts a competing SQLite write (`BEGIN IMMEDIATE` on the same thread DB) and records whether it acquired the lock. Used to prove no write transaction is held across a provider call (stronger than a bare delay).\n    12\t  - `spyProvider()` — records every call; used to assert **zero** provider calls in compact paths.\n    13\t- **Verification tiers** are the existing `red-verify` / `verify` / `green-verify` / `verify-all`; no new scripts.\n    14\t- **First-pass config defaults** used by tests (dial-in values, not architecture):\n    15\t  - `smoothing.maxInferenceTokens = 4000`\n    16\t  - `toolResult.tiers = { small: 1000 → 0.10–0.20, mid: 5000 → 0.02–0.05, large: >5000 → truncate }`\n    17\t\n    18\t## Config defaults under test\n    19\t\n    20\t| Setting | First-pass value | Tuned in |\n    21\t|---|---|---|\n    22\t| smoothing length cap | 4000 tokens | next epic |\n    23\t| tool-result large-tier threshold | 5000 tokens | next epic |\n    24\t| tool-result tier targets | 10–20% / 2–5% / truncate | next epic |\n    25\t\n    26\t---\n    27\t\n    28\t## TC → Test Mapping\n    29\t\n    30\t### Flow 1 — Prompt Smoothing → `test/smoothing-recovery.test.ts`\n    31\t\n    32\t| TC | AC | Setup | Assertion |\n    33\t|---|---|---|---|\n    34\t| TC-1.1a | 1.1 | prompt with irregular whitespace, deterministic provider spy | cleaned whitespace; provider not called for the deterministic stage |\n    35\t| TC-1.1b | 1.1 | over-cap prompt | deterministic cleaning still applied |\n    36\t| TC-1.2a | 1.2 | under-cap prompt | `smoothPrompt` invoked; its output stored |\n    37\t| TC-1.2b | 1.2 | over-cap prompt, provider spy | `smoothPrompt` NOT invoked; deterministic result stored |\n    38\t| TC-1.3a | 1.3 | prompt with fenced code + typo-laden prose, real-ish passthrough | fenced block byte-identical; prose changed |\n    39\t| TC-1.4a | 1.4 | over-cap prompt | derivation state `ready` (not \"skipped\"/\"degraded\") |\n    40\t| TC-1.4b | 1.4 | under-cap, inference ok | state `ready` |\n    41\t| TC-1.5a | 1.5 | `failingProvider({ smoothPrompt: retryable })` | state `pending`, item requeued |\n    42\t| TC-1.5b | 1.5 | smoothing `pending`, consume via compose | deterministic floor used, no block |\n    43\t| TC-1.6a | 1.6 | intake a prompt, provider spy | no provider call during intake; smoothing item queued |\n    44\t| TC-1.7a | 1.7 | `failingProvider` exhausts budget | state `failed` with reason; not `ready` |\n    45\t| TC-1.7b | 1.7 | `failed` smoothing, consume via compose | deterministic floor used via cascade |\n    46\t\n    47\t### Flow 2 — Tool-Result Rendering → `test/tool-result-rendering.test.ts`\n    48\t\n    49\t| TC | AC | Setup | Assertion |\n    50\t|---|---|---|---|\n    51\t| TC-2.1a | 2.1 | large tool result past visibility boundary | deterministic truncation, no provider call, identical input → identical output |\n    52\t| TC-2.2a | 2.2 | tool result in smooth-band turn | summary produced by queued inference item, not hot path |\n    53\t| TC-2.3a | 2.3 | result < 1000 tokens | small-tier target applied |\n    54\t| TC-2.3b | 2.3 | result 1000–5000 tokens | mid-tier target applied |\n    55\t| TC-2.3c | 2.3 | result > 5000 tokens | truncated, not inference-summarized |\n    56\t| TC-2.4a | 2.4 | results from two tools | per-tool guidance keyed in prompt; outcome preserved both |\n    57\t| TC-2.4b | 2.4 | failed tool result | summary states failure outcome |\n    58\t| TC-2.5a | 2.5 | turn with a tool call | no `tool_call_summary` derivation exists or is queued |\n    59\t| TC-2.5b | 2.5 | tool call in rendered turn | call args present as recorded, no summary step |\n    60\t| TC-2.6a | 2.6 | result truncated (full band) + summarized (smooth) | original full result intact in record |\n    61\t| TC-2.7a | 2.7 | result > 5000 tokens | `tool_result_summary` is the truncation, state `ready`, no inference item created |\n    62\t| TC-2.8a | 2.8 | in-threshold result, `failingProvider` exhausts | state `failed` with reason; truncation floor used by consumers |\n    63\t\n    64\t### Flow 3 — Turn Construction and Recovery Cascade → `test/turn-cascade.test.ts`\n    65\t\n    66\t| TC | AC | Setup | Assertion |\n    67\t|---|---|---|---|\n    68\t| TC-3.1a | 3.1 | turn with smoothed prompt `ready` | smoothed prompt used as-is |\n    69\t| TC-3.2a | 3.2 | smoothed prompt `pending`, no re-derive | deterministic-cleaned prompt used; turn constructs |\n    70\t| TC-3.2b | 3.2 | smoothed prompt `failed` | same cascade as pending; usable component |\n    71\t| TC-3.2c | 3.2 | floor unproducible | original source used |\n    72\t| TC-3.3a | 3.3 | `tool_result_summary` not ready | truncation used, never raw full result |\n    73\t| TC-3.4a | 3.4 | turn with assistant text, thinking, runtime-change block | verbatim, in order |\n    74\t| TC-3.5a | 3.5 | turn with multiple not-ready derivations | construction completes; every component present |\n    75\t| TC-3.6a | 3.6 | smoothed prompt floored | log entry: derivation type, subject id, reason, floor |\n    76\t| TC-3.6b | 3.6 | all derivations ready | no fallback log entries |\n    77\t| TC-3.7a | 3.7 | re-derivation of a not-ready component, `probingProvider` | the competing write acquires its lock while the provider call is pending → no write transaction held across the call |\n    78\t| TC-3.8a | 3.8 | `failed` component (no live work item) re-derived successfully | `recoverDerivation` persists; row now `ready` with re-derived content |\n    79\t| TC-3.8b | 3.8 | `pending` component (no live item) resolved to floor | row `ready` with floored content via `recoverDerivation`, no degraded marker, fallback logged |\n    80\t| TC-3.8c | 3.8 | tool-result summary unready, unrecoverable | floor written back is truncation, never raw |\n    81\t| TC-3.8d | 3.8 | race: `failed`/`pending` component **with a claimed work item present** (DD-4) | `recoverDerivation` returns `persisted:false`; row left untouched; the turn rendering still used the floor; a later worker completion writes the real `ready` and is not clobbered |\n    82\t\n    83\t### Flow 4 — Chunk Derivation and Compact Recovery → `test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts`\n    84\t\n    85\t| TC | AC | Setup | Assertion |\n    86\t|---|---|---|---|\n    87\t| TC-4.1a | 4.1 | chunk closes | detailed + brief = two separate work items |\n    88\t| TC-4.1b | 4.1 | detailed ok, brief fails | states independent (`ready` / `failed`) |\n    89\t| TC-4.2a | 4.2 | compact needs a `failed` detailed summary, `spyProvider` | `compactChunkMaterial` returns stored-member concat; **zero provider calls** (compact never models) |\n    90\t| TC-4.3a | 4.3 | summary unrecoverable at compact | band entry = deterministic concat of stored members; no missing span |\n    91\t| TC-4.4a | 4.4 | compact performs a fallback | visible warning naming what fell back |\n    92\t| TC-4.4b | 4.4 | compact mid-assembly, stop requested | halts without corrupting thread |\n    93\t| TC-4.5a | 4.5 | multiple missing/failed summaries | compact completes with concat fallbacks, not failure |\n    94\t| TC-4.5b | 4.5 | corrupt canonical source for a span | `compactChunkMaterial` returns `blocked`; compact refuses with `state_corruption` |\n    95\t| TC-4.6a | 4.6 | compact over not-ready summaries, `spyProvider` | **zero** provider calls during the entire compact |\n    96\t| TC-4.7a | 4.7 | compact falls back to concat | log entry: chunk, derivation type, reason, fallback |\n    97\t| TC-4.8a | 4.8 | background chunk summary, member `lower_band_projection` `pending` | summary work requeues (waits) with reason `member_projection_not_ready` — not concat, not `failed`, not a provider-failure reason |\n    98\t| TC-4.8b | 4.8 | member turn source corrupt | background summary surfaces source problem |\n    99\t\n   100\t### Flow 5 — Derivation Logging → `test/logging-surface.test.ts`\n   101\t\n   102\t| TC | AC | Setup | Assertion |\n   103\t|---|---|---|---|\n   104\t| TC-5.1a | 5.1 | write at info/warning/error | all three persisted with level |\n   105\t| TC-5.2a | 5.2 | write from internal + external caller | both land via same method/store |\n   106\t| TC-5.3a | 5.3 | derivation fell back | subject + rendering carry no degraded flag; fallback event only in log |\n   107\t| TC-5.3b | 5.3 | derivation terminally failed | derivation record shows `failed` + reason, independent of log |\n   108\t| TC-5.4a | 5.4 | mixed entries | query by level + derivation type returns only matches |\n   109\t| TC-5.5a | 5.5 | logging store write fails during turn construction | construction completes; logging failure contained |\n   110\t\n   111\t### Flow 6 — Runtime-Change Typing → `test/runtime-change-typing.test.ts`\n   112\t\n   113\t| TC | AC | Setup | Assertion |\n   114\t|---|---|---|---|\n   115\t| TC-6.1a | 6.1 | model-change runtime event at intake | typed `model_change` block with previous + new model |\n   116\t| TC-6.2a | 6.2 | thinking-level-change event at intake | typed `thinking_level_change` block with previous + new level |\n   117\t| TC-6.3a | 6.3 | turn with model change then thinking change | both typed blocks verbatim, in order |\n   118\t\n   119\t---\n   120\t\n   121\t## Architecture-Risk Tests (named)\n   122\t\n   123\t| Risk | TC(s) | What it proves |\n   124\t|---|---|---|\n   125\t| Source-truth preserved | TC-2.6a | full tool result intact under truncation + summary |\n   126\t| No-txn-across-provider (turn recovery) | TC-3.7a | competing write acquires lock during provider call |\n   127\t| Compact makes no provider call | TC-4.2a, TC-4.6a | `spyProvider` observes zero calls |\n   128\t| Recovery write-back defers to live work | TC-3.8d | claimed item present → floor does not persist; worker wins |\n   129\t| Stale recovery discarded | TC-3.8a (+ version-bump variant) | `recoverDerivation` is version-checked; stale discards |\n   130\t| Dependency-wait classified correctly | TC-4.8a | reason `member_projection_not_ready`, not provider failure |\n   131\t| Log never rolls back work | TC-5.5a | logging failure contained, turn still completes |\n   132\t| Idempotent background wait | TC-4.8a | requeue-and-wait does not duplicate work |\n   133\t| Tier/cap boundaries | TC-2.3c/2.7a, TC-1.2b | threshold edges behave |\n   134\t| Rename safety | Story 0 gate | rename is behavior-preserving (`verify-all` green under renamed vocabulary); `tool_call_summary` removal is a separate behavior change with its own red/green |\n   135\t| Corruption blocks | TC-4.5b | only canonical source corruption stops a compact |\n   136\t\n   137\t---\n   138\t\n   139\t## Per-Chunk Red/Green Exit Criteria\n   140\t\n   141\t| Chunk | Red exit | Green exit |\n   142\t|---|---|---|\n   143\t| 0 — rename + logging | renamed tree compiles; logging skeleton present; existing tests reference new names and fail only on logging-not-implemented | suite green under renamed vocabulary; TC-5.1a–5.5a pass. (`tool_call_summary` is renamed-but-retained here; its removal is Chunk 2.) |\n   144\t| 1 — smoothing floor | smoothing tests red on missing deterministic stage/gate | TC-1.1a–1.7b pass |\n   145\t| 2 — tool-result tiers + `tool_call_summary` removal | tier-gate + removal tests red (`tool_call_summary` still present) | TC-2.1a–2.8a pass; `tool_call_summary` gone from kind set/registry/`PART_PLANS`/provider |\n   146\t| 3 — cascade + logging | write-back + fallback-log tests red | TC-3.1a–3.8c pass |\n   147\t| 4 — chunk/compact recovery | background-wait + compact stored-member concat fallback (no model) tests red | TC-4.1a–4.8b pass |\n   148\t| 5 — runtime typing | typed-block projection tests red | TC-6.1a–6.3a pass |\n   149\t\n   150\t## Coverage Confirmation\n   151\t\n   152\t- 39 ACs, 59 TCs, every TC mapped to a test file and assertion above.\n   153\t- Every AC has ≥1 TC (verified against `epic.md`).\n   154\t- Mock boundary: `DerivationProvider` only; all storage real.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
